INFO:  GPORCA failed to produce a plan, falling back to Postgres-based planner
DETAIL:  Falling back to Postgres-based planner because GPORCA does not support the following feature: UPDATE or DELETE using ctid without gp_segment_id
ERROR:  DELETE uses system-defined column "t.ctid" without the necessary companion column "t.gp_segment_id" (cdbmutate.c:327)
HINT:  To uniquely identify a row within a distributed table, use the "gp_segment_id" column together with the "ctid" column.
DEALLOCATE del_ctid;
CREATE FUNCTION del_by_ctid(tid) RETURNS void LANGUAGE plpgsql AS
  $$ BEGIN DELETE FROM t WHERE ctid = $1; END $$;
SELECT del_by_ctid('(0,1)');
